key.quote:
The King—with lawful triumph—took his fame,
But not his country, from Mahendra's king,
And set him free;

As rain from Heaven is one, yet forms diverse
In various lands assumes, so Thou, unchanged
In essence, workest various;

Youth, power, and beauty,—each alone breeds pride;
And all in him were met, yet his great heart
Swelled not with pride unduly.

